CLEAR
-----
Resets or erases the current value or setting for the specified option.

  Syntax:

  CL[EAR] {option}

  Options:

  BRE[AKS]    Removes the break definition set by the BREAK command. 
  BUFF[ER]    Clears text from the buffer. CLEAR BUFFER has the same effect as CLEAR SQL, unless multiple buffers are in use.
  COL[UMNS]   Resets column display attributes set by the COLUMN command to default settings for all columns.
  COMP[UTES]  Removes all COMPUTE definitions set by the COMPUTE command.
  CONTEXT     Clears the context.
  SCR[EEN]    Clears the screen.
  SQL         Clears the text from SQL buffer. CLEAR SQL has the same effect as CLEAR BUFFER, unless multiple buffers are in use.
  TIMI[NG]    Deletes all timers created by the TIMING command


  Examples:

  To clear breaks, enter:
    SQL> CLEAR BREAKS

  To clear column definitions, enter:
    SQL> CLEAR COLUMNS
